ZTS: pass the TSRMLS context to the lexers in the shipped parsers

The pre-generated Bison parsers in the release tarball were produced without
ZTS: their YYLEX macro calls yylex(&yylval) with no thread context, while both
zendlex() and ini_lex() are declared with TSRMLS_DC. The ZTS build therefore
fails with "too few arguments to function 'zendlex'". YYLEX_PARAM cannot help
here: the .y files declare it in %code requires, which Bison emits into the
generated *header*, and the .c never sees it.

TSRMLS_CC expands to nothing without ZTS, so passing it unconditionally keeps
the non-threaded build working unchanged.

--- a/Zend/zend_language_parser.c
+++ b/Zend/zend_language_parser.c
@@ -2804,7 +2804,7 @@
 #ifdef YYLEX_PARAM
 # define YYLEX yylex (&yylval, YYLEX_PARAM)
 #else
-# define YYLEX yylex (&yylval)
+# define YYLEX yylex (&yylval TSRMLS_CC)
 #endif
 
 /* Enable debugging if requested.  */
--- a/Zend/zend_ini_parser.c
+++ b/Zend/zend_ini_parser.c
@@ -939,7 +939,7 @@
 #ifdef YYLEX_PARAM
 # define YYLEX yylex (&yylval, YYLEX_PARAM)
 #else
-# define YYLEX yylex (&yylval)
+# define YYLEX yylex (&yylval TSRMLS_CC)
 #endif
 
 /* Enable debugging if requested.  */
